-- title:
--   Lifting an invariant compatible family of chart functions to sections
-- statement:
--   The setting is the Čerednik–Drinfeld formal uniformisation tower, with all data given explicitly as hypotheses.
--
--   **Arithmetic base.** A prime $r$; a domain $\mathcal O$ of characteristic zero which is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`), an irreducible element $\pi$, with $\mathcal O$ complete for the $\pi$-adic topology (`hcomplete`), residue field of cardinality $r$ (`hres`), and $r$ generating the same ideal as $\pi$ (`hunr`, an unramifiedness normalisation); a characteristic-zero field $K_0$ which is the fraction field of $\mathcal O$.
--
--   **Unramified extension.** A characteristic-zero domain $Onr$ over $\mathcal O$ and an $\mathcal O$-algebra automorphism $Fr$ of $Onr$, subject to: $Onr$ is complete for the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$ (`hOnr_complete`), that ideal is maximal (`hOnr_max`), every element of $Onr$ satisfies a monic polynomial over $\mathcal O$ modulo that ideal (`hOnr_alg`), every monic polynomial over $Onr$ of positive degree has a root modulo that ideal (`hOnr_closed`), and $Fr(x)\equiv x^{r}$ modulo that ideal for all $x$ (`hFr`) — so $Fr$ reduces to the Frobenius. A homomorphism $vdet \colon GL_2(K_0)\to\mathbb Z$ (written multiplicatively) with `hvdet`: $vdet(g)=n$ if and only if $\det g = u\pi^{n}$ for some unit $u$ of $\mathcal O$; that is, $vdet$ is the $\pi$-adic valuation of the determinant.
--
--   **Group data.** A group $G$, a homomorphism $\sigma\colon G\to GL_2(K_0)$, a subgroup $\Gamma$ containing a scalar element $z$ with $vdet(\sigma z)=2$ (`hcent`) and an element $w$ with $vdet(\sigma w)=1$ (`hodd`), and a subgroup $\Gamma'$ characterised by `hΓ'` as the elements of $\Gamma$ at which $vdet\circ\sigma$ is even. A homomorphism $\rho\colon G\to PGL_2(K_0)$ with $\rho =$ the projectivisation of $\sigma$ (`hρ`), such that the image of $\Gamma'$ in $PGL_2(K_0)$ acts on the vertices of the Bruhat–Tits tree of $\mathcal O$, $K_0$ with finite stabilisers (`hdisc`) and with finitely many orbits (`hcocpt`). The matrix $g_1$ is the diagonal matrix $\mathrm{diag}(\pi,1)$ (`hg₁`). A subgroup $N \le \rho(\Gamma')$ (`hNle`) whose preimage in $\rho(\Gamma)$ is normal (`hNnorm`) and of nonzero relative index in $\rho(\Gamma')$ (`hNidx`), and a `MumfordTower` $DM$ for $(\mathcal O,\pi,K_0,r,g_1,N)$: a tower of schemes $DM.Z\,n$ over $\mathcal O/\pi^{n+1}$, flat and proper, cartesian along the transition maps, with affine neighbourhoods of finite sets, together with an $N$-invariant natural family of maps $DM.q$ classifying Deligne data, and charts.
--
--   **The tower $X$ and its Frobenius-twisted structure.** Schemes $X\,n$ with structure maps $xb\,n$ to $\operatorname{Spec}(\mathcal O/\pi^{n+1})$, transitions $xt\,n$, a finite group $G_2$ acting by $a\,n$, and a pair of projections $pr_1\,n \colon X\,n\to DM.Z\,n$ and $pr_2\,n$ to the spectrum of $E/\pi^{n+1}E$, where $E$ is the equalizer subalgebra of $Fr^2$ and the identity on $Onr$ (the quadratic unramified subextension). A homomorphism $\theta\colon\Gamma\to G_2$ and automorphisms $Fr_2\,n$ of $E/\pi^{n+1}E$. The hypotheses on this data are: each square $(xt\,n, xb\,n, xb(n+1))$ is cartesian over $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the quotient map (`hcart`); $xb\,n$ is proper (`hproper`) and flat (`hflat`); finite subsets of $X\,n$ lie in affine opens (`haff`); $G_2$ acts over the base (`ha_over`) and compatibly with the transitions (`ha_xt`); $X\,n$ is the fibre product of $DM.Z\,n$ and $\operatorname{Spec}(E/\pi^{n+1})$ over $\operatorname{Spec}(\mathcal O/\pi^{n+1})$ via $pr_1, pr_2$ (`hX`), with the compatibilities $xb\,n = pr_1\,n$ followed by $DM.zb\,n$ (`hxb`) and the two transition compatibilities (`hxt₁`, `hxt₂`); $\theta$ is surjective (`hθsurj`) with kernel the elements of $\Gamma$ mapping into $N$ (`hθker`); $Fr_2\,n$ is induced by $Fr$ (`hFr₂`); the action of $\theta(\gamma)$ on the second factor is by $Fr_2^{-vdet(\sigma\gamma)}$ (`ha_pr₂`); and the action of $\theta(\gamma)$ on the first factor transports Deligne data by $\sigma(\gamma)^{-1}$ in the sense of `DeligneDatum.IsPullback` (`ha_pr₁`).
--
--   **Quotient data.** A `TowerQuotientDatum` $DQ$ for $(\mathcal O,\pi,X,xb,xt,G_2,a)$, that is, a tower $DQ.Y$ over $\mathcal O/\pi^{n+1}$, proper and flat, cartesian in $n$, together with a finite surjective $G_2$-invariant map $DQ.p\,n\colon X\,n\to DQ.Y\,n$ satisfying the listed descent and local-universal properties. A family $q$ of maps $\operatorname{Spec} B\to DQ.Y\,n$ defined on pairs (an $\mathcal O$-algebra map $Onr\to B$, a Deligne datum over $B$) for $B$ killed by $\pi^{n+1}$, subject to: $q$ is computed from $DM.q$ and $pr_2$ through $DQ.p$ (`hqdef`), lies over $\operatorname{Spec} B\to\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ (`hqover`), is natural in $B$ (`hqnat`), compatible with the transitions $DQ.yt$ (`hqyt`), and invariant under the twisted action of $\sigma(\gamma)$, $\gamma\in\Gamma$, in the sense of `OmegaNr.IsTwistedAct` — twisting the $Onr$-point by $Fr^{-vdet}$ and pulling back the Deligne datum by $\sigma(\gamma)^{-1}$ (`hqinv`).
--
--   **Unramified layer.** An `NrPresentation` $Pr$ of the above over $Onr$ with distinguished subgroup the image under $\theta$ of $\Gamma'\cap\Gamma$, giving a tower $Pr.X'$ over $Onr/\pi^{n+1}$, a $G_2$-action $Pr.a'$, a map $Pr.qX$ to $X$ realising $X'$ as base change, and charts $Pr.\kappa'\,h\,n$ from the spectrum of $A_n := \mathrm{chartERing}(Onr,\pi,r)/\pi^{n+1}$ (the localisation of the edge relation quotient away from the discriminant, reduced mod $\pi^{n+1}$) into $Pr.X'\,n$. A `TowerQuotientDatum` $D'$ for the tower $Pr.X'$ over $Onr$, together with maps $rY\,n\colon D'.Y\,n\to DQ.Y\,n$ exhibiting $D'.Y\,n$ as the base change of $DQ.Y\,n$ along $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the quotient map $\mathcal O/\pi^{n+1}\to Onr/\pi^{n+1}$ (`hrY`), compatible with the projections (`hrY_p`) and the transitions (`hrY_yt`).
--
--   **Charts on the quotient.** For each $h\in GL_2(K_0)$ and $n$, an open $U\,h\,n$ of $D'.Y\,n$ whose underlying set is the image of the topological map of $Pr.\kappa'\,h\,n$ followed by $D'.p\,n$ (`hU`); a ring homomorphism $c\,h\,n$ from the sections of $D'.Y\,n$ over $U\,h\,n$ to $A_n$, the preimage of $U\,h\,n$ under that composite being all of $\operatorname{Spec} A_n$ (`hκU`), and $c\,h\,n$ being the pullback of sections along that composite, read through the canonical isomorphism $\Gamma(\operatorname{Spec} A_n)\cong A_n$ (`hc`).
--
--   **The given family.** A fixed $h\in GL_2(K_0)$ and elements $fam\,m \in A_m$ for all $m$, compatible under the transition maps $A_{m+1}\to A_m$ (`hfam`). The invariance hypothesis `hinv` requires: for every $m$, every $\mathcal O$-algebra and $Onr$-algebra $B$ (with compatible scalars) in which the image of $\pi$ is nilpotent, every pair of $Onr$-algebra maps $\bar x,\bar x'\colon A_m\to B$ and Deligne data $d,d',P,P'$ over $B$, if $d$ lies in the standard edge chart determined by $\bar x$ — its line at the standard full lattice is spanned by $\bar x(\xi)\otimes e_0 + 1\otimes e_1$, its line at $g_1$-translate of that lattice is the image under $actBaseChange$ of the span of $1\otimes e_0 + \bar x(\eta)\otimes e_1$, and $d$ satisfies `InEdgeChart` for the pair of lattices — and $d'$ satisfies the same three conditions with $\bar x'$ in place of $\bar x$, and if $P$ (resp. $P'$) is the pullback of $d$ (resp. $d'$) along $h^{-1}$, and if there exists $\gamma\in\Gamma'$ with $P'$ the pullback of $P$ along $\sigma(\gamma)^{-1}$, then $\bar x(fam\,m) = \bar x'(fam\,m)$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** There exists a family of sections $s\,m \in \Gamma(U\,h\,m, \mathcal O_{D'.Y\,m})$ for all $m$, such that:
--
--   (i) for every $m$ and every witness that $U\,h\,m \le (D'.yt\,m)^{-1}(U\,h\,(m+1))$, the restriction to $U\,h\,m$ of the pullback of $s(m+1)$ along $D'.yt\,m$ equals $s\,m$ — the family is compatible along the tower; and
--
--   (ii) for every $m$, $c\,h\,m(s\,m) = fam\,m$ — the family induces the given chart functions.
--
--   This is the existence half of the correspondence between invariant compatible chart functions and compatible sections over the chart opens; no uniqueness is asserted.
--
--   This is the existence statement in the construction of functions on the unramified layer of the Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation tower: a compatible family of functions on the standard edge chart, invariant under the relevant $\Gamma'$-identifications, descends to a compatible family of sections of the quotient tower over the chart open. It is used by [`CerednikDrinfeld.FormalOmega.descendedQuotientMap_nrFunctions`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.FormalOmega.descendedQuotientMap_nrFunctions), and is proved from the general gluing principle [`AlgebraicGeometry.TowerQuotientDatum.exists_sections_eq_of_forall_specMap_comp_eq`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.TowerQuotientDatum.exists_sections_eq_of_forall_specMap_comp_eq) together with the chart transition and overlap-agreement results for the unramified presentation.
